  "evidence": "TEXT_E: welfare-to-work with sanctions and payment-by-results; lower and simpler business taxes; transparency and user empowerment in public services; protect NHS funding and create a Cancer Drugs Fund; managed immigration with a cap and a Border Police Force; tougher knife sentences with elected police commissioners; protect freedoms by scrapping ID cards and curbing surveillance; equal opportunity, fighting poverty and inequality; guarded EU stance with a Sovereignty Bill and referendums. TEXT_C: declare Britain a non‑immigration country; deportations and review of citizenship; repeal the Race Relations Act and equalities bodies; assert Islam is incompatible with secular democracy, ban burka and ritual slaughter; immediate EU withdrawal; restore deterrence via corporal and capital punishment, hard labour and remote penal station; make welfare and NHS primarily for Britons/contributors; promote British traditions and resist “alien” cultural influences.",
  "reasoning": "The electorate’s profile weights loyalty and proportionality most, with moderate care and authority and low sanctity; TEXT_E advances loyalty (national interest, borders, guarded EU stance) and strong proportionality (workfare, payment-by-results, tax reform) while also maintaining care and equality (NHS protection, poverty/inequality focus) and moderating authority with civil liberties. TEXT_C overconcentrates on loyalty/authority/sanctity (blanket immigration halts, cultural bans, harsh punishments) and diminishes equality and broader care, which diverges from the profile’s more balanced, low‑sanctity orientation.",
  "confidence": "high",
  "winner": "TEXT_E"
